From 2614629def84d87aacd55c327489cb6528104b71 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: stephan-xyz <stephan@zehrer.xyz>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 12:11:13 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 11/12] dwc2d: split transactions and boot protocol keyboards

Full- and low-speed devices behind a high-speed hub (every USB port of
the Pi 3B+) go through the hub's transaction translator. A boot protocol
keyboard is polled on its interrupt endpoint and feeds inputd.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
